# Lore

Lore is Risto's private knowledge: who Risto is, how Risto works, and what Risto knows about each project.
It is the entry point for agents and for Risto. "Update lore" means write it here.

Each folder is its own private git repo. Which ones are cloned depends on the machine:

{{ range (splitList "," (index . "loreRepos" | default "")) -}}
{{- $repo := trim . -}}
{{- if $repo -}}
- `{{ $repo | base }}/`
{{ end -}}
{{- end }}
Each repo's `readme.md` states its scope, what never goes in it, and its layout. Read it
before writing there.

## Where writes go

- Anything that holds in every context (who Risto is, preferences, conventions, general tool knowledge):
  `global/`. "Global" means on every machine; it is still private.
- Work for an employer or a project: that repo.
- Unsure: the narrower repo. Moving content toward a broader repo can leak for good, while the
  reverse is safe to fix later.

## Code repos

Notes for a code repo sit in the lore repo for its scope, usually at `repos/<code-repo>/`, with an
upstream page `repos/<code-repo>.md` (its remote URL and local path). Lore is the only source: where a
checkout still has a `.llms/` folder, it's a generated copy (see its `GENERATED.md`), so edit lore instead.

chezmoi writes this file from `~/.local/share/chezmoi/lore/readme.md.tmpl`.
